Now add camera occlusion to game.js. After camera position computed, before setting camera.position. Use camSmooth as target. We want segment from camSmooth to (cx,cy,cz). Sample 10 steps. For each, check colliders near. But we should only consider colliders with height relevant. Use camR.

Potential issue: camera starts at ground and tree near; if collider overlaps line, pull in. Good.

Add method:

```
  cameraBlockT(x0,z0,x1,z1) {
    const world = this.world;
    if (!world?.grid) return 1;
    const cell = world.cell;
    const steps = 10;
    for (let i=1;i<=steps;i++){
      const t = i/steps;
      const x=x0+(x1-x0)*t, z=z0+(z1-z0)*t;
      const gx=Math.floor(x/cell), gz=Math.floor(z/cell);
      for (let ox=-1;ox<=1;ox++) for (let oz=-1;oz<=1;oz++) {
        const arr=world.grid.get((gx+ox)+','+(gz+oz));
        if(!arr) continue;
        for (const c of arr) {
          const rr = c.camR ?? c.r;
          if (Math.hypot(x-c.x,z-c.z) < rr) return Math.max(0.22, t - 0.6/steps);
        }
      }
    }
    return 1;
  }
```

Then in updateCamera:

```
const block = this.cameraBlockT(this.camSmooth.x,this.camSmooth.z,cx,cz);
if (block < 1) {
  cx = this.camSmooth.x + (cx-this.camSmooth.x)*block;
  cz = this.camSmooth.z + (cz-this.camSmooth.z)*block;
  cy = this.camSmooth.y + (cy-this.camSmooth.y)*block;
}
```

Need recompute ground after? cy could go below ground? If pulled in, cy lower but target y ~1.55, so above ground. Then clamp ground again.

We could also reduce distance by occlusion. Let's add.

Also important: when camera is inside canopy but the 2D segment passes through a tree, yes.

